WEBVTT

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:23.140
In this wide world

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:28.320
People you're meant to meet can be seen

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:34.900
Beyond the window, beyond the rainbow

00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:38.530
I think you're aware of them

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:45.640
Take off that restrictive weight

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.610
Let your feelings go

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:55.920
Now keep your ears open and wait for that time

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:58.680
Awaken now

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:11.970
Cherish the little dream you've
drawn in the vast sky

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:19.240
If you do, you can always become happy

00:01:19.240 --> 00:01:22.010
It's certain

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:26.380
Woh woh

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.060
It's starting to get pretty cold, huh?

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:45.600
Yes, it is.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.830
Humans are so sensitive to the elements.

00:01:49.540 --> 00:01:53.410
He might even catch a cold
wearing such light clothing.

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:58.880
You say you want to take a few days off
from class, starting tomorrow?

00:01:58.880 --> 00:01:59.850
Yes...

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:04.280
Well, with the grades you get, I don't think
taking a few days off will set you back much.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:06.250
Do you think so?

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:12.850
Okay, time to get started...

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:19.430
Ah! The Beleaguered Queen of Vengeance!

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:31.470
Christmas is...

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:33.010
Let's have a nice, quiet
Christmas Eve at a restaurant
Miss Mishima, this Christmas won't you
please form a search party with me

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.520
that serves a full course
reindeer dinner, Rosanjin-style...
to go search the mountains of
Finland for Santa Claus?

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.990
Please come with me to Nekomi Cathedral
to listen to Christmas carols!
...is a time when I, the
Queen of NIT, shine my brightest.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.980
Let's spend a "midsummer Christmas" on the
beach in Australia splitting watermelons!
...is a time when I, the
Queen of NIT, shine my brightest.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.650
M-Miss Mishima!

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.760
Yes, they all want to be chosen by me!

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:51.170
But for some reason it's unfulfilling...

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:53.470
Deep down inside, I'm not satisfied.

00:02:53.470 --> 00:02:57.040
What in the world could I be lacking?

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.770
What's up, Sayoko!

00:02:58.770 --> 00:03:00.540
Good morning, Morisato!

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:01.470
What the...

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:04.050
Morning, Kei-chan!

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.650
Hey. Morning.

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:08.670
Don't tell me Belldandy's given
you the cold shoulder.

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.350
Sheesh, are you going to start
giving me that, too?

00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:14.060
Well, that's what everyone is thinking!

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.180
After only two days?

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:18.960
It just goes to show how close
the two of you are.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.860
Oh, man is it warm over here or what?

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.530
Give it a rest!

00:03:22.530 --> 00:03:24.430
Yikes! You're so scary!

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:27.900
I've got it.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:31.570
Now I know what to do to fill
this emptiness I'm feeling.

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:35.740
There's but one man at this university
who I have been unable to conquer...

00:03:35.740 --> 00:03:37.550
Keiichi Morisato,

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:42.680
my heart will surely be content
once you are mine!

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:53.530
C'mon, Big Sister, when are you
going to be done with that?

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.400
I'll be done real soon.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:56.430
Aww...

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:59.630
That's ALL you've been doing lately!

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:01.600
I'm sorry, Skuld.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:05.040
Once it's finished, I'll make some
ice cream for you, okay?

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:08.140
But, still, a goddess among
goddesses like you

00:04:08.140 --> 00:04:13.710
could make a hand-knitted sweater in an
instant if she just used her powers.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:20.020
Dance! Mingle and entwine along
with me, and become one!

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:23.160
You see?

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:25.590
Who the heck would wear THAT?!

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:26.960
Leave this to me!

00:04:27.660 --> 00:04:30.200
It's the fully automatic hand-knitting
machine, Amigo-01!

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:33.130
With this little number, you'll have
your sweater lickety split!

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:36.040
"Fully automatic" would mean it's
no longer HAND-knitted, you know...

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.710
Oh, shut up!

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.330
Switch on!

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:41.840
Done!

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:42.880
Wah! Big Sister!

00:04:42.880 --> 00:04:44.980
What the heck is she doing?
Wah! Big Sister!

00:04:44.980 --> 00:04:45.780
Wah! Big Sister!

00:04:45.780 --> 00:04:48.580
When you knit, you can't
simply "make" things.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:54.920
There are all kinds of feelings and
memories that go into your knitting.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:56.990
You knit so that every one of them

00:04:56.990 --> 00:05:00.220
will give warmth to the person
who wears what you make.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:04.060
I don't really get that kind of stuff...

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:06.870
That sweater looks like it'll
be nice and warm.

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:08.270
Thanks!

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:14.810
Say, why are you keeping this
sweater a secret anyway?

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:19.250
Well, it's because I thought that
this way it would be...

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.220
more of a surprise to Keiichi.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:25.490
What is it?

00:05:25.820 --> 00:05:28.120
Well, it's just that you've certainly become

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:32.290
a lot like an ordinary Earth girl
since you came down here.

00:05:33.030 --> 00:05:35.550
I've become like a human?

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:37.730
I see...

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.060
I'm home!

00:05:39.270 --> 00:05:40.730
Keiichi!

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.840
Welcome home!

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:46.670
So Belldandy wants to
surprise him, does she?

00:05:48.810 --> 00:05:51.040
This is kinda complicated...

00:05:52.250 --> 00:05:55.280
Hey, so like, you got dumped
by Belldandy, huh?

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:57.150
Could be...

00:05:57.150 --> 00:05:58.150
How can you be so laidback about it?!

00:05:58.150 --> 00:06:00.290
No, it's not like that!

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:01.790
Is this seat taken?

00:06:01.790 --> 00:06:02.790
Sayoko?

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.660
Looks like you've got some time on your
hands, sitting here by yourself.

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:07.160
Looks like you do, too, for the same reason.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:08.690
N-No, I don't!

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:12.070
So anyway, it's getting pretty close
to Christmas, isn't it?

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:15.570
Wouldn't you like to spend a
wonderful evening with me?

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:18.770
We could rent out a 5-star hotel
and have a big party

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:21.780
or take a luxury liner on a cruise
around Tokyo Bay.

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:25.340
It'd be such a letdown to be alone
on Christmas Eve of all nights!

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:29.680
I'm flattered that you'd be
so concerned for me.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.480
But I'll be okay.

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:33.290
What do you mean?

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:39.160
She's been with me all this time and
gone to lot of trouble for me,

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:42.460
so I need to give her some time
to herself for once, too.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:46.070
Well it looks like you sure have
a lot of trust in her.

00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:49.760
And I wonder what she's doing
with this "time."

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:55.000
You don't suppose... she's doing something
like what we are right now.

00:06:56.140 --> 00:06:58.750
I guess I never thought about that!

00:06:58.750 --> 00:07:01.120
I... I'm only joking, obviously!

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.220
If Belldandy were that kind of girl,

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:05.980
then I wouldn't have to go through
this much trouble to...

00:07:08.290 --> 00:07:12.260
You really do trust Belldandy with
that kind of thing, don't you?

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:15.960
That's the kind of thing I kinda
like about you, Sayoko.

00:07:16.700 --> 00:07:20.330
She always puts others before herself,

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:23.700
so I'm glad she's doing something for herself.

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:28.680
It's also fun for me to imagine Belldandy
as I haven't seen her,

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:31.280
like doing whatever she's doing now,

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:32.410
He's boasting about her?
Morisato of all people?
Like doing whatever she's doing now,

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:35.220
He's boasting about her?
Morisato of all people?
Or whatever she's thinking...

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:40.240
So you don't have to worry, because
it's not so bad being on my own.

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:43.190
Things are probably much tougher for you,

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:45.790
since you always have lots
of people around you.

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:49.960
I'm sure you have to keep them
in mind all the time.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:54.400
Belldandy and I will be just fine.

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:58.170
I haven't said anything offensive, have I?!

00:07:58.170 --> 00:07:59.230
No...

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:01.980
Oh, it's almost time for my lecture!

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:02.880
Huh?

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:05.110
I appreciate your concern.

00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:09.850
It's made me realize that it's what's
in a person's heart that counts.

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:18.980
You couldn't drink me under the
table in a million years.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:22.800
Men are a total snooze.

00:08:22.800 --> 00:08:25.270
They're just way too dull!

00:08:25.570 --> 00:08:30.770
How could a guy turn a girl down
after having her go so far?

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:32.140
Is that normal?!

00:08:32.710 --> 00:08:35.180
Hey, are you listening?

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:39.040
Sheesh!

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:47.450
What does he mean "it's what's in
a person's heart that counts"?

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:50.650
What the heck would I know about that?

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:53.860
After all, no one's ever said anything
like that to me before.

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:55.260
Why?

00:08:55.260 --> 00:08:59.300
Why do the words and the
smile of a guy like that

00:08:59.300 --> 00:09:03.000
have to make a queen like me feel
like such a piece of crap?

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:06.670
Morisato, you damn stinkin' jerk!

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:14.780
Huh?

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:17.340
There's someone on the roadside...

00:09:18.720 --> 00:09:20.120
Sayoko?!

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.520
Ah, it's Morisato!

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:26.230
And she's totally drunk.

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:29.230
You'll catch a cold if you fall asleep
in a place like this!

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:31.060
Morisato!

00:09:32.730 --> 00:09:36.500
Woo-hoo! I'm all over Morisato...

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:38.370
Whoa, Sayoko!

00:09:38.610 --> 00:09:42.040
Hey, listen. You know what?

00:09:42.040 --> 00:09:44.240
I really think you're...

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:46.350
Huh?

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:48.120
Oh, no.

00:09:48.120 --> 00:09:50.480
NO, DON'T!

00:09:56.260 --> 00:10:00.130
What am I doing here?

00:10:01.730 --> 00:10:04.630
Ah, my head's killing me...

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:06.760
Guess I drank a little too much.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:10.630
Is this... Morisato's place?

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:15.640
I don't believe that guy...

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:21.380
Please wait just a little longer, Keiichi.

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:30.490
For crying out loud! So in the end,
that's all she's doing, huh?

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:35.130
What's she looking so happy for when
she's only knitting like that?

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:36.360
Finished!

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:46.270
I've woven my feelings into every
thread of this sweater...

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:49.400
I hope that it will keep Keiichi
nice and warm.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:55.440
Keiichi.

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:03.090
Big Sister? You were looking for
some wrapping paper, right?

00:11:03.420 --> 00:11:06.130
Look, I found some that's perfect!

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:08.060
Oh, my! Thank you.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:10.390
I'll use it right away then.

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:13.700
Hey, come here a second!

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:14.970
Is something the matter?

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:17.440
Oh, what now?!

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:35.390
At your age you should be able to
zip up your own clothes in the back!

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:38.420
Nothing wrong with that.
I'm just the touchy feely type.

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:39.690
Huh?

00:11:39.690 --> 00:11:40.660
It's gone!

00:11:41.130 --> 00:11:42.300
It's gone!

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:45.600
Keiichi's... sweater.

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:49.860
She's gone!

00:11:50.640 --> 00:11:52.130
Why...

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:08.160
Stealing that sweater from you
was just way too cruel!

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:11.030
Well, we're not certain that she did.

00:12:11.030 --> 00:12:14.630
But it's not like the sweater walked
out of here on its own either.

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:16.000
But...

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:19.530
There was only one person by the
sweater when it disappeared.

00:12:19.530 --> 00:12:22.530
And she vanished before we knew it.

00:12:22.900 --> 00:12:26.270
That's right! I can't think of anyone
else who'd have done it!

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:28.540
She is not a bad person.

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:29.910
But still!

00:12:29.910 --> 00:12:31.880
You can say that if you like, but...

00:12:33.080 --> 00:12:36.070
I've got an idea! The birdies might
have seen something.

00:12:36.920 --> 00:12:38.750
Tell me, birdie.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:44.390
You say a doggie went off with
the package in his mouth?

00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:47.860
Why would a dog have taken the sweater?

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:50.030
All he said was that it had a tasty scent.

00:12:50.030 --> 00:12:51.130
Gulp!
All he said was that it had a tasty scent.

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:51.500
All he said was that it had a tasty scent.

00:12:51.500 --> 00:12:53.300
A tasty scent?

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:55.470
Stop right there.

00:12:55.470 --> 00:12:56.770
Why are you sneaking off?

00:12:57.670 --> 00:12:59.210
I get it now.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:03.110
The dog was attracted by the scent of the
wrapping paper and made off with the package.

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:05.350
That's right! It's the dog's fault!

00:13:05.350 --> 00:13:07.250
WHOSE fault did you say that was?

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:09.150
Ow! That hurts!

00:13:09.150 --> 00:13:10.720
I'm sorry!

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:12.780
I'll be sure to give you your
punishment in full later.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:15.850
I'm going to go search for it!

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:17.680
Belldandy!

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:24.830
It's just knitting.

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:27.690
Even I should be able to do it...

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:35.610
It's not like he's going to be happy over
something he can't see the feeling in.

00:13:38.410 --> 00:13:42.580
I wonder if he'd be happy over
something I knitted for him.

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:47.590
Oh, I give up!

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:03.300
Stop!

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:09.980
Hand-knitting is just plain silly nowadays!

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:13.450
That's right!

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:16.750
As long as the price is right, anyone
will wag their tail for me!

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:23.190
Hello, there's something I'd like you
to make for me on short notice.

00:14:23.190 --> 00:14:25.780
No, the price is not a concern.

00:14:27.660 --> 00:14:32.530
Morisato's got to be like other guys!

00:14:33.070 --> 00:14:35.930
Excuse me, I have a question
if you don't mind.

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:39.060
Have you seen a package like this?

00:14:40.980 --> 00:14:42.780
I see...

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:44.570
Well, thank you.

00:14:45.450 --> 00:14:47.410
Excuse me, Sunfishy?

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:50.280
Have you seen a package like this?

00:14:53.750 --> 00:14:54.850
Thank you...

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.380
Thank you...

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:03.760
Morisato.

00:15:04.370 --> 00:15:06.660
Sayoko? You okay now?

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:09.970
Yes, all thanks to you.

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:13.640
Well I couldn't get the smell off, actually!

00:15:13.640 --> 00:15:15.080
What are you talking about?

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:17.010
Oh, nothing.

00:15:17.610 --> 00:15:22.050
I see... It looks like I was a huge
burden on you yesterday, huh?

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:24.180
I'm telling you not to worry about it!

00:15:24.180 --> 00:15:27.350
After all, Belldandy's the one
who looked after you.

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:29.820
Oh. I don't remember that.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:32.960
How about I repay you by treating you

00:15:32.960 --> 00:15:36.000
to a banquet of French Court cuisine
aboard a luxury liner?

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:38.500
Sorry, but I can't do dinner with you.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:41.840
Why not? Don't you want to eat with me?

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:46.040
Nah, it's because I'm sure that Belldandy
already has something ready and waiting for me.

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:49.340
Come eat with us sometime!
Her cooking's great!

00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:55.380
You're always going on about her...

00:15:55.380 --> 00:15:57.750
Okay, then we could do something
other than dinner, right?

00:15:57.750 --> 00:15:59.590
Well... I guess so.

00:15:59.590 --> 00:16:01.090
Then let's go!

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:01.920
Whoa...

00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:03.450
Come on, already!

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:09.050
All this searching and still nothing...

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:12.860
But I won't give up!

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:17.770
Because that sweater holds my feelings.

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:22.210
Will you accept that as some
small token of gratitude?

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:27.050
I never would have guessed that that retro car
shop is run by the Mishima conglomerate.

00:16:27.050 --> 00:16:30.070
Thanks to that, I got to see their
prized collection of models.

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:32.350
It's my father's hobby.

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:35.090
That's where he bought those model
cars from a while back.

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:38.390
That was a terrible thing you did!

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:43.060
I got chewed out by my father after all that.
C'mon, cut me some slack!

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:54.470
It's fun just to walk along
with him like this...

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:59.580
It gives me this strange kind of feeling.

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:06.620
Say, how do you think the two of us
look to other people right now?

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:08.520
Good question...

00:17:08.520 --> 00:17:11.720
Like a queen and her retainer maybe?

00:17:12.390 --> 00:17:14.620
Hey, I'm only joking!

00:17:15.600 --> 00:17:18.800
I guess we look like a couple of friends.

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:20.270
Friends?

00:17:20.700 --> 00:17:23.000
A lot has happened between you and me,

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:26.110
but now we can talk to each
other on normal terms.

00:17:26.110 --> 00:17:29.130
It's also in part because I met Belldandy.

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:32.780
If I hadn't, then I'd be the same
old person I used to be,

00:17:32.780 --> 00:17:36.410
and we probably wouldn't be able to walk
around together like we are now.

00:17:37.220 --> 00:17:39.620
What's with this guy?

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:43.150
He doesn't have a clue as to how girls feel.

00:17:48.030 --> 00:17:50.330
Hey, Morisato?

00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:51.690
What's up?

00:17:52.030 --> 00:17:54.500
I'd like you to have this.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:57.500
It's a Christmas present from me to you.

00:17:57.500 --> 00:18:01.100
Isn't it kind of a waste to give that to me?

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:02.980
Why?

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:05.510
It's a high quality cashmere sweater!

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:09.070
You'd never be able to get one with
the part-time wages you make!

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:12.390
I... can't take it.

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:14.220
Why not?

00:18:14.220 --> 00:18:16.020
It's nothing big.

00:18:16.420 --> 00:18:19.760
I told you. It's what's in a
person's heart that counts.

00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:22.300
Are you saying my heart
doesn't make the cut?!

00:18:22.300 --> 00:18:24.300
It's not like that at all!

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:27.530
Because you've put your feelings into that gift.

00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:31.770
Maybe it's because I'm always with Belldandy...

00:18:31.770 --> 00:18:34.170
but that's the feeling I get about you.

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:40.940
So I think you should give that to someone you
really want to express your feelings towards.

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:45.420
I see...

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:48.290
Oh, I give up!

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:51.620
I just can't hang around with you guys at all!

00:18:52.230 --> 00:18:53.750
Sayoko...

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:56.290
Huh?

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:58.530
I picked that up on the side of the road.

00:18:58.530 --> 00:19:01.400
I was thinking I'd throw it away,
but I'll give it to you instead!

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:04.900
If you tell me you won't take this
either, then I'll hit you!

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:07.410
But, this is...

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:11.380
Just put it on and wear it home;
you'll understand soon enough.

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:14.350
I'm sure she's looking all over for it...

00:19:17.650 --> 00:19:19.210
Go on home!

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:21.480
Right...

00:19:35.970 --> 00:19:37.530
Miss Sayoko!

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:41.740
Are you feeling better now?

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:43.540
You had me worried.

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:46.980
It looks like you've been searching
the whole time, huh?

00:19:47.310 --> 00:19:51.410
But your feelings should be getting
across to him right about now.

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:54.050
Are you talking about the sweater?

00:19:54.050 --> 00:19:55.680
So you know about it?

00:19:56.120 --> 00:19:59.850
Yeah. I stole it from your house.

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:03.190
I really wanted to just throw it out.

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:06.890
But I couldn't do it.

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:11.610
Because you're not that kind of person.

00:20:11.610 --> 00:20:13.110
Oh, can it!

00:20:13.110 --> 00:20:17.370
I don't want to hear that crap from you!

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:19.610
Okay...

00:20:22.120 --> 00:20:23.320
Belldandy.

00:20:23.320 --> 00:20:24.280
Yes?

00:20:24.590 --> 00:20:28.820
I am Sayoko Mishima,
Queen of NIT.

00:20:28.820 --> 00:20:30.620
Who the heck are you?

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:36.190
I am Belldandy, Goddess 1st Class,
2nd Category, Unlimited License.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:38.030
Oh...

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:43.690
You know... I hate your guts.

00:20:44.610 --> 00:20:48.540
I love you very much, Miss Sayoko.

00:20:49.340 --> 00:20:51.310
Well, if you'll excuse me...

00:20:57.890 --> 00:20:59.440
Liar...

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:05.260
You're no goddess, knitting a sweater
for Morisato like you did.

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:09.460
You're just an ordinary girl.

00:21:12.230 --> 00:21:14.260
I'm home.

00:21:15.570 --> 00:21:17.570
Oh, Big Sister!

00:21:17.570 --> 00:21:20.630
Here, c'mon, Keiichi! Hurry up!

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:23.140
Welcome home, Belldandy.

00:21:24.210 --> 00:21:26.200
We've been waiting for you.

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:29.640
My feelings...

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:32.210
They came across to you!

00:21:32.450 --> 00:21:34.250
Oh, Keiichi!

00:21:38.290 --> 00:21:39.990
I'm so glad!

00:21:41.160 --> 00:21:44.760
Your feelings came across to me just fine.

00:21:48.170 --> 00:21:49.970
It's nice and warm.

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:06.590
It's all right.

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:09.090
Because I am the Queen, after all.

00:22:09.090 --> 00:22:14.030
Morisato, if you think I've given up,
you are sorely mistaken.

00:22:14.030 --> 00:22:17.030
Someday, I'll get even with you

00:22:17.030 --> 00:22:20.160
for humiliating me like you have.

00:22:25.270 --> 00:22:33.700
Woh, it starts to shine

00:22:43.190 --> 00:22:50.490
The gentle wind I felt on my cheek

00:22:51.830 --> 00:22:59.260
Was the start of the miracles you brought

00:22:59.940 --> 00:23:07.400
As though my everyday life until
then had never existed

00:23:07.780 --> 00:23:13.020
My new happy life, completely repainted

00:23:13.020 --> 00:23:16.420
In the colors of spring

00:23:17.090 --> 00:23:21.360
Even waking up early, even traffic jams

00:23:21.360 --> 00:23:25.770
Even heavy things to carry,
even sleepless nights

00:23:25.770 --> 00:23:30.100
Somehow I feel thankful for everything

00:23:30.100 --> 00:23:34.810
Let's create more and more of our miracles

00:23:34.810 --> 00:23:42.650
Woh, whatever kind of morning

00:23:43.420 --> 00:23:51.150
Woh, it starts to shine

00:23:51.860 --> 00:23:54.660
Every day is a miracle

00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:59.330
He tries so hard to return the
feelings of his goddess.

00:23:59.330 --> 00:24:00.930
The goddess believes in him,

00:24:00.930 --> 00:24:02.840
and continues waiting all alone
for him to come home.

00:24:02.840 --> 00:24:04.740
Next time, "Ah! I Offer These Feelings
on Christmas Eve!"

00:24:04.740 --> 00:24:06.170
Ah! I Offer These Feelings on Christmas Eve!
Next time, "Ah! I Offer These Feelings
on Christmas Eve!"

00:24:06.170 --> 00:24:09.340
Ah! I Offer These Feelings on Christmas Eve!
It's what's in a person's heart that
matters most... isn't it?
